*.crt

# AI Assistant — intentionally excluded from the published repo, at every depth
# (unanchored on purpose, unlike the anchored scratch-script rules below).
# NOTE: finpal_core/CLAUDE.md carries real contributor conventions (repository
# pattern, the "do not do" list). Those belong in a tracked CONTRIBUTING.md
# before open-sourcing — do not just un-ignore this file.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# Shell scripts — root-level utility/deployment scripts only
/*.sh
# backup/ scripts must remain tracked
!backup/entrypoint.sh
!backup/backup-pg.sh

# Ad-hoc test and check scripts — root-level only.
# These MUST stay anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `test_*.py` matches
# recursively and silently excluded the entire tests/ suite, and
# `simplefin_*.py` excluded src/modules/pointspal/simplefin_bridge.py.
/test_*.py
/simplefin_*.py
/simplefin_*.json

# Data files
app.db


# Docker
.docker

# Server-specific / operational compose files (not for repo)
docker-compose.demo.yml
docker-compose.local.yml
docker-compose.override.yml

# Jupyter Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints

# Archive folder (old code reference)
_archive/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~.nib

# Dockerfile-generated files
ssl_fix.py
temp_app.py

# node — web-ui's dependencies, at any depth. NOT previously listed, which meant
# `git add -A` in this repo would have committed the whole tree to a PUBLIC
# repository. Nothing was ever tracked from it; this closes the door.
node_modules/

# Design scratch that must never reach the published repo. Both directories were
# DELETED on 2026-08-09 by owner instruction; the rules stay so that re-creating
# either one cannot reach a commit.
#
# *** THESE WERE PROTECTED ONLY BY A SENTENCE IN CLAUDE.md *** — "screenshots/ is
# untracked and must stay that way; `git add -A` picks it up, stage explicitly."
# That is a discipline problem doing a .gitignore's job, and screenshots/ alone is
# 20 MB. A rule you can forget twice belongs here instead. Added 2026-08-09.
screenshots/
monarch/
